+// Lobium: a profile launched with a fingerprint config registers no speech-recognition,
+// on-device-translation or WASM-TTS component.
+//
+// These four are not small. Measured on 152.0.7977.42, a single freshly launched profile that is
+// left alone downloads 824 MB, of which SODA (112 MB), SODALanguagePacks (194 MB), TranslateKit
+// (78 MB) and WasmTtsEngine (23 MB) account for 407 MB installed plus 385 MB of the
+// component_crx_cache that holds their CRXs - 792 MB of the 824. Every profile is its own
+// --user-data-dir, so that cost is paid again per profile.
+//
+// Nothing is bought with it. Probed over CDP on a profile that had all four fully installed:
+// speechSynthesis.getVoices() is 0, and Translator / LanguageDetector are not even defined - the
+// same values a profile that never downloaded them reports. No web-visible surface changes, so on
+// a product that sells many concurrent profiles this is pure per-profile disk.
+//
+// Deliberately narrower than --disable-component-update, which would also drop CRLSet,
+// First-Party Sets, Privacy Sandbox attestations and Origin Trials. Those total ~32 MB and DO
+// shape web-visible behaviour, so they stay registered and keep tracking real Chrome.
+bool LobiumSuppressesHeavyComponents() {
+  return base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch("lobium-fp-config");
+}
